ponent. If you win, target creature gains double strike until end of turn. (Each clashing player reveals the top card of their library, then puts that card on the top or bottom. A player wins if their card had a higher mana value.)', "Whenever Surgespanner becomes tapped, you may pay {1}{U}. If you do, return target permanent to its owner's hand.", 'Whenever Veteran of the Depths becomes tapped, you may put a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Whenever a Forest enters the battlefield under your control, Battlewand Oak gets +2/+2 until end of turn.\\nWhenever you cast a Treefolk spell, Battlewand Oak gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Whenever a Goblin you control is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, you may put a +1/+1 counter on Knucklebone Witch.', 'Whenever a Merfolk you control becomes tapped, you may gain 1 life.', "Whenever a creature with toughness 4 or greater is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, you may exile it.\\nAt the beginning of the end step, if three or more cards have been exiled with Colfenor's Urn, sacrifice it. If you do, return those cards to the battlefield under their owner's control.", "Whenever a nontoken creature you control attacks, you may pay {W}. If you do, create a 1/1 white Kithkin Soldier creature token that's tapped and attacking.", 'Whenever a player casts a Giant spell, you may put a +1/+1 counter on Elvish Handservant.', 'Whenever a player casts a Kithkin spell, you may have target player lose 1 life.', 'Whenever an attacking Kithkin or Elf is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a blue spell during your turn, you may create a 4/4 green Elemental creature token.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell, that player draws seven cards.', 'Whenever another Goblin you control is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, you may have Boggart Shenanigans deal 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.', "Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, you may put X +1/+1 counters on Hamletback Goliath, where X is that creature's power.", 'Whenever another nontoken Elf is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, you may create a 1/1 green Elf Warrior creature token.', 'Whenever you activate an ability of an Elemental, Ceaseless Searblades gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "Whenever you activate an ability, if it isn't a mana ability, you may pay {2}. If you do, copy that ability. You may choose new targets for the copy.", 'Whenever you cast a Treefolk spell, you may have target creature get +3/-3 until end of turn.', "Whenever you cast a spell during an opponent's turn, you may have each opponent lose 1 life.", 'Whenever you cast an Elf spell, you may create a 1/1 green Elf Warrior creature token.', 'Whenever you clash and win, you may draw a card. (This ability triggers after the clash ends.)', "Whenever you clash, tap target creature an opponent controls. If you won, that creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step. (This ability triggers after the clash ends.)", 'Whenever you clash, you may pay {1}. If you do, create a 3/1 red Elemental Shaman creature token. If you won, that token gains haste until end of turn. (This ability triggers after the clash ends.)', 'Whenever you draw a card, you may put a hoofprint counter on Hoofprints of the Stag.\\n{2}{W}, Remove four hoofprint counters from Hoofprints of the Stag: Create a 4/4 white Elemental creature token with flying. Activate only during your turn.', 'You lose 2 life and draw two cards, then clash with an opponent. If you win, repeat this process. (Each clashing player reveals the top card of their library, then puts that card on the top or bottom. A player wins if their card had a higher mana value.)', 'You may activate abilities of creatures you control as though those creatures had haste.\\n{1}, {T}: Untap target creature.', 'You may choose new targets for target instant or sorcery spell. Then copy that spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.', "[+1]: Chandra Nalaar deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\n[−X]: Chandra Nalaar deals X damage to target creature.\\n[−8]: Chandra Nalaar deals 10 damage to target player or planeswalker and each creature that player or that planeswalker's controller controls.", '[+1]: Target player discards a card.\\n[−2]: Search your library for a card, then shuffle and put that card on top.\\n[−8]: Put all creature cards from all graveyards onto the battlefield under your control.', '[+1]: Untap two target lands.\\n[−1]: Create a 3/3 green Beast creature token.\\n[−4]: Creatures you control get +3/+3 and gain trample until end of turn.', '[+1]: You gain 2 life.\\n[−1]: Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control. Those creatures gain vigilance until end of turn.\\n[−6]: Create a white Avatar creature token. It has "This creature\'s power and toughness are each equal to your life total."', '[+2]: Each player draws a card.\\n[−1]: Target player draws a card.\\n[−10]: Target player mills twenty cards.', "{1}, Sacrifice Wanderer's Twig: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.", '{1}, {T}: You may cast a spell from your hand without paying its mana cost if it has the same name as a spell that was cast this turn.', '{1}{R}: Put a +1/+1 counter on Ashling the Pilgrim. If this is the third time this ability has resolved this turn, remove all +1/+1 counters from Ashling the Pilgrim, and it deals that much damage to each creature and each player.', '{1}{U}, {T}: You may tap or untap target creature.', '{1}{W}: Prevent all damage that would be dealt to target tapped Merfolk or Kithkin creature this turn.', '{2}: Target creature gains trample until end of turn. If this is the third time this ability has resolved this turn, you may add {R}{R}{R}{R}{R}{R}{R}{R}.', '{2}{B}, Exile an Elf card from your graveyard: Scarred Vinebreeder gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', '{2}{B}: Regenerate target Treefolk.', '{2}{R}: Creatures you control get +1/+0 until end of turn. If this is the third time this ability has resolved this turn, creatures you control gain first strike until end of turn.', '{3}, Sacrifice Herbal Poultice: Regenerate target creature.', '{3}{R}: Flamekin Spitfire deals 1 damage to any target.', '{B}, Sacrifice a Goblin: Facevaulter gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', '{G}, {T}: Look at the top two cards of your library, then put them back in any order.', '{G}, {T}: Target attacking creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', '{R}, Sacrifice Boggart Forager: Target player shuffles their library.', '{R}: Flamekin Brawler gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{T}, Discard an Elf card: Target creature gets -X/-X until end of turn, where X is the number of Elves you control.', '{T}, Sacrifice a Goblin: Tar Pitcher deals 2 damage to any target.', '{T}, Tap an untapped creature you control: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add two mana in any combination of colors. Spend this mana only to cast Elemental spells or activate abilities of Elementals.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add {G}.', '{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature for each Elf you control.', '{T}: Target Goblin creature you control gets +1/+0 and gains flying until end of turn. Sacrifice that creature at the beginning of the next end step.', "{T}: Target Merfolk creature gets +1/+1 and gains islandwalk until end of turn. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\n{T}: Target land becomes an Island until end of turn.", '{T}: Target creature gets -X/-0 until end of turn, where X is the number of Merfolk and/or Faeries you control.', '{T}: Target land becomes the basic land type of your choice until end of turn. Activate only during your turn.', '{T}: Until end of turn, target Forest becomes an X/X Treefolk creature in addition to its other types, where X is the number of Elves you control.', "{U}: Deeptread Merrow gains islandwalk until end of turn. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", '{W}, {T}: Harpoon Sniper deals X damage to target attacking or blocking creature, where X is the number of Merfolk you control.', '{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.']
flavor: ['"A good day in Goldmeadow is one in which I don\'t spend all evening picking quills out of my backside."\\n—Calydd, kithkin farmer', '"A ribbon torn will ward away dark dreams."', '"After Auntie brushed the soot from her eyes, she discovered something wonderful: the fire had turned the goat into something that smelled delicious."\\n—A tale of Auntie Grub', '"All the sylvan secrets of this world are etched between my rings. The skinfolk\'s metal aberrations can rot between my roots."\\n—Colfenor, the Last Yew', '"And though she didn\'t get her honey, Auntie found something far more interesting."\\n—A tale of Auntie Grub', '"Any dream is a robust harvest. Still, I prefer the timeworn dreams, heavy with import, that haunt the obsessive mind."', '"Apply orange leaf to a wound at dawn to clean it, at dusk to prevent the same injury from happening again."\\n—Kithkin superstition', '"As far as I can tell, that frog dangling from the stick serves absolutely no purpose whatsoever."\\n—Gaddock Teeg', '"Auntie Grub had caught a goat, a bleating doe that still squirmed in her arms. At the same time, her warren decided to share with her a sensory greeting of hot tar . . . ."\\n—A tale of Auntie Grub', '"Auntie pointed out to the faerie how much mischief a flying boggart could wreak, and a beautiful new friendship was born."\\n—A tale of Auntie Grub', '"Be silent and listen to your inner fire. Only then can you walk the Path of Flame."', '"Beauty determines value, and we determine beauty."', '"Better to flare out than to gutter."\\n—Flamekin expression', '"Boom! Boom! Boots the size of oxcarts, then an axe like a falling sun. Elves scattered. Trees scattered. Even the hills ran for the hills!"\\n—*Clachan Tales*', '"By tradition, we don\'t speak for two days after battle. If our deeds won\'t speak for themselves, what else could be said?"', '"Clever folk build their homes near cloudcrowns. If a hawk or even just a faerie tries to swoop in, it\'ll get swatted from here to Cloverdell."\\n—Calydd, kithkin farmer', '"Each year that passes rings you inwardly with memory and might. Wield your heart, and the world will tremble."', '"First it was plovers and mulldrifters. Now it\'s knitting needles the size of javelins."\\n—Calydd, kithkin farmer', '"How do the vinebred feel? Fah! We do not ask the puppet how it feels when the puppeteer bids it dance."', '"I bring baubles of lore, lost secrets seined from the listening waves."', '"I don\'t know why the little one was so mad. He said to put him down, and I put him down."', '"I knew that trick long before your great-grandmother\'s great-grandmother was born."', '"I\'ve gotten close enough to a giant to smell his breath, but none has ever so much as spotted me. I wonder how long my record can extend?"', '"If a boggart even dares breathe near one of my kin, I\'ll know. And I\'ll not be happy."', '"If one can associate any virtue with the eyeblights, it is the talent some achieve in disposing of them. I have seen the slaying of boggarts raised nearly to an art form."\\n—Fiala, Gilt-Leaf winnower', '"If there\'s a place worth going, the Merrow Lanes already do. And if there\'s a route worth taking, yours truly already has."', '"If you live on a giant\'s back, there\'s only one individual you\'ll ever need to fear."\\n—Gaddock Teeg', '"If you want to test wisdom, offer it to fools and watch how they tear it up."', '"It\'s a proven fact that sling-stones from the dawn side of the riverbank sail the farthest and truest."\\n—Deagan, cenn of Burrenton', '"May you shade three generations of seedlings."', '"Most faeries are harmless pranksters. Every now and again, though, you get one that crosses over from mischievous to malicious."\\n—Gaddock Teeg', '"My ears say it hisses. My fingers say it burns."\\n—Auntie Wort', '"My success at navigating the Dark Meanders irritates the Inkfathom school. They consider themselves peerless divers, but I try to remind them that they cannot own commodities like bravery and cunning."', '"No matter how adept our artistic skill, our effigies can never hope to capture the vibrant beauty of a living elf. Perhaps that is truly why we mourn."', '"None appreciate sun and shallows like those who have seen the depths."\\n—Lianda of the Stonybrook school', '"Petals within petals within petals, tadpole. The truth lurks below an opulence of illusion."\\n—Neerdiv, fallowsage', '"Reach in this hole, lose a hand. Reach in that hole, find a sparkly."\\n—Auntie wisdom', '"Roam as you will, your roots remain in the strong earth of your Rising."', '"Springjacks and faeries can be difficult to hunt, but my favorite prey are the flamekin. They never fail to put up a worthy fight when cornered."', '"The changing kind suffers as we do. We must join as one to quench our tyrants!"', '"The elves may try to confine us, but they will learn that our blazing spirit can never be suppressed."\\n—Vessifrus, flamekin demagogue', '"The elves use treefolk to drive us away. It is time to remove their tools."\\n—Vessifrus, flamekin demagogue', '"The unpredictable fae are just as likely to provide a blight as a boon."\\n—Desmera, perfect of Wren\'s Run', '"Things were popping like corn in a skillet. Olly landed in the pig pen with his prize sow on top of him, both squealin\' like boggarts."\\n—Deagan, cenn of Burrenton', '"This vulgar mimicry will end now."\\n—Desmera, perfect of Wren\'s Run', '"Those without beauty are Lorwyn\'s greatest tumor. The winnowers have an unpleasant duty, but a necessary one."\\n—Eidren, perfect of Lys Alana', '"Thoughtweft binds us together as one, part of an intricate pattern that would unravel if even one thread came loose."', '"Tie a mouse under a bridge, and your cabbages will triple in size."\\n—Kithkin superstition', '"Water is in the air, the trees, and the earth. Understand its motion, speak its language, and the subtle currents that flow through all living things will fall under your command."', '"We are a clachan of smiths. The forge is as comfortable to us as a small fire during a cool winter\'s evening."', '"We look in the river and see scattered stones. A merrow looks and sees a map of Lorwyn."\\n—Illulia, flamekin soulstoke', '"We merrows need not be disadvantaged when fighting on land. We lack the vulnerability of those who breathe only through their throats."\\n—Minnarin, merrow reejerey', '"We see the same sky as you, just through a different lens."', '"What do they need all this stuff for? They\'re dead. We\'re alive. Simple enough."', '"What does a mountain fear of a fly? Giants are barely aware of us, let alone afraid."\\n—Gaddock Teeg', '"When merrows talk, listeners grow fins."\\n—Kithkin saying', '"Which is more filled with poison: the flower of the moonglove or the minds of elves?"\\n—Vessifrus, flamekin demagogue', '"Why do our pies squeak? It\'s all the faeries, mice, and prickly-hogs we stuff inside."\\n—Borb of the Squeaking Pie warren', '"Without flame, there would be no iron tools, no cooked meals, no purge of old growth to make room for new."\\n—Brighthearth creed', '"You\'ve discovered that boggarts bite, I see. And will the militia be chasing this lot? . . . Ah, you\'re staying in town to avoid Nath\'s hunt. Wise. Now this poultice . . ."', 'A changeling involuntarily mimics the nearest being at hand, sometimes trading a borrowed shell for borrowed claws.', 'A circle of sugar and a word of forbiddance.', 'A giant can brood over a grudge for decades, and woe to those who interrupt him.', 'A hundred generations has he mentored, a hundred armies has he crushed beneath his feet, yet only a hundred words has he ever spoken, each more revered than a hundred books.', 'A light an army can follow.', "A savage hunter with a prince's bearing.", 'After trying mudskippers for an afternoon, Scratch decided that crickcarp made the best noise.', "Although they're protective of all creatures, many treefolk are especially fond of the empathic kithkin.", 'Among the boggarts, there is only one real rule: all new treasures and experiences must be shared. Those who hoard their gifts commit the one truly unforgivable sin.', 'Among the solitude-loving giantkind, teamwork is unusual. But he appreciates hearing the occasional "Swing down and to your left."', "An elvish duel is a thing of beauty: the warriors' grace, the crash of steel, then the artful spray of blood.", 'At night, the faeries steal dreamstuff for their queen. At daybreak, countless creatures wake weak and hollow.', "Auntie Flint lent axes to Nibb and Gyik, thinking they'd share their experiences with her. She's still waiting for them to come back.", 'Auntie Flint was the first to pioneer the spiderwig, a mass of arachnids intended to be worn rather than eaten.', 'Auntie always knows which berries to lick, which kithkin to trick, and what to do when either goes wrong.', 'Auntie excitedly held up the squalling newborn. "This one looks like Byoog! Maybe he\'ll tell us what he saw and felt in the beyond."', 'Because of their capricious nature, faeries can serve as living lenses for disruptive magic.', 'Below the great river, a bustling hub channels the flow of merrow trade.', "Beneath the fae's constant pranks runs a subtler undercurrent of mockery: the influence of Oona, their hidden queen.", 'Boggarts constantly strive to outdo each other with the things they bring back to the warren, each hoping the exploit will become as well-known as those of Auntie Grub.', "Boggarts get so excited when they find something new to smash that they really don't notice who gets underfoot.", 'Boggarts revel in discovering new sensations, from the texture of an otter pellet to the squeak of a dying warren mate.', 'Bulgo paused, puzzled. What was that rustling sound, and why did he feel so stiff? And how could his *feet* be so thirsty?', 'Calm as a wisent\'s watch\\n—Elvish expression meaning "safe"', 'Changeling magic grants unusual wishes.', 'Changelings can alter shape based on what the beings around them desire most.', 'Changelings cannot resist the draw of a new shape, even if doing so would be in their best interests.', "Dawn's Light, greatest palace of Gilt-Leaf Wood, is built on tiers of wood and power.", 'Deep in Glen Elendra blossoms Oona, queen of the faeries, nourished by secrets and pollinated by stolen dreams.', 'Desmera blinded her seers so that her beauty would be the last image burned in their memories. The act only deepened their insight.', 'Diluted, moonglove can etch living tissue. Concentrated, a drop will kill a giant.', "Each bone honors its owner's best pranks.", "Eidren's hunts are dangerous affairs. All dread the inevitable recounting of those who died while flushing out his prey.", 'Eidren, perfect of Lys Alana, ordered hundreds of trees uprooted and rearranged into a pattern he deemed beautiful. Thus the Gilt-Leaf Wood was born.', 'Elementals are ideas given form. This one is the idea of "smashitude."', 'Elves of the immaculate class weave flora into living creatures—sometimes to endorse an elite warrior, sometimes to create a breathing work of art.', 'Elvish battle-magic has evolved two specialties: inflicting wounds that scar, and healing wounds without scarring. Politics determines the recipients of each.', "Even the oldest treefolk was but an acorn when Lorwyn's first mysteries were born.", "Even when a giant's tantrum turns the sky into a chaotic gale, the path of the balloonist never falters.", 'Faeries hang beings that interest them as ornaments in the sky, each clique competing to outshine the prize of the last.', 'Fallowsages debate whether the whiskergill is native to the Dark Meanders or merely dreamstuff made real.', 'Five-toed grave\\n—Kithkin phrase meaning "a giant\'s footprint"', "Flamekins' fires burn cool until they decide otherwise.", 'For disfigured elves, there are few choices beyond death or nettlevine.', 'For every tree who falls, there are countless sprouts waiting to rise.', 'From mite to mighty.', "From the highest tiers of Dawn's Light Palace to the deepest shade of Wren's Run, the silver notes of the horn shimmer through the air, and all who hear it feel its pull.", 'He cares not for the disasters his storm brings as long as his path ahead is clear.', 'He paints with drop and shimmer a world that exists only in the wistful heart.', 'Her ears are open to even the softest voice.', "His home clachan's familial spirit bolsters his own, but he will be ready to preside over the town as cenn only after he learns to project that strength to others.", 'If you pick a fight with one kithkin, be ready to fight them all.', 'In a culture of beauty, the most beautiful are worshipped as gods.', 'In a world of bright, cloudless skies, she is the dark storm on the horizon.', 'In beauty-obsessed Lys Alana, one cut of her blade means the difference between a high society feast and raking through the dungheap for scraps.', 'In desolate places, changelings may take the shape of fancies, or memories, or fears.', 'In his presence, an ordinary grove becomes a bastion to turn spells and break armies.', 'In the backwaters of the Merrow Lanes lie stones scarred with tallies of countless generations, each representing a victory of merrow soldiers.', 'It absorbs the pain of other treefolk, which leaves it bitter, yet addicted to the sensation of agony.', "It hoards Lorwyn's rare sorrows.", "It takes a huntmaster's eye to discern the contours of mythical prey.", 'It takes two to craft a mirror: a practiced metalsmith to silver one side and her own hazy reflection to polish the other.', "Just as a changeling's influence can have dramatic effects, so too can its sudden withdrawal.", "Kith goats are just for practice. The real prize, of course, is a giant's cloudgoat.", 'Kithkin weave together their very thoughts, creating a depth of cooperation unknown to other races.', 'Leave it to a boggart to come up with a projectile as disgusting as it is deadly.', 'Like being trapped in a perpetual sneeze, faerie-dust poisoning is both exhilarating and agonizing.', "Lorwyn's stones resonate with the place from which they were hewed. Though taken far, still they call to their home when silence is upon the land.", 'Made from whiskergill bones, merrow spinebows can fire bolts through tree trunks.', 'Memories of ages past are said to swim the minds of lounging fallowsages.', "Merrows consider themselves the keepers of Lorwyn's past—and consider it their duty to edit when necessary.", 'Mined from a cave in the Dark Meanders, it shines brightest when no one is looking.', "Once each year, the sun's rays reach the hidden chamber of Velis Vel, and the changelings congregate from afar to bathe in the ever-shifting light.", 'One glamer leads him far from home. The next washes away his memory that home was ever anywhere but at her side.', 'One good mimic deserves another.', 'One part cunning, one part wise, and many, many parts demented.', 'One whiff of the sweet, pungent scent leads to euphoria—or to an early grave.', "Paradoxically, to tilt the massive jug for a sip, you'd need the energy of the giant's tonic.", "Pretty, valuable, and delicious—a boggart thief's trifecta.", 'Protected by glamers and guile, Glen Elendra harbors the elusive Oona, queen of the fae.', "Schools meet and mingle on Lorwyn's riverways. In the bustling interplay, the merrow renew their sense of community as they sharpen their wits and hone their trading skills.", 'Skilled merrow rudders ensure their charges arrive on time and without incident.', "Smik learned the elvish dance quickly enough. The most difficult, yet most important step was to stay out of Nath's sight until called to perform.", 'Snokk ran as fast as he could, but the sound of hooves grew ever louder in his ears.', 'So great is his wisdom and spirit that many who have met him say that they stood before a giant of a man and talked to the wisest of the four winds.', 'Some flamekin warriors explore the art of coherence, an ancient discipline that harnesses the chaos of fire and focuses it with pinpoint precision.', "Some say the valley of Glen Elendra is mythical, and that rumors of its existence are nothing but a faerie prank. Others say it is the fae's most fiercely guarded secret.", 'Sometimes a curious giant singles out a "little one" to follow for a few days, never realizing the effect it will have on the little one\'s life.', 'Steady and silent as the deep current, the reejerey guides the course of the school.', "Thanks to one champion archer, the true borders of Kinsbaile extend an arrow's flight beyond the buildings.", "The Silvergill school monitors traffic on the Lanes, ensuring that the riffraff don't interfere with travelers.", "The Stinkdrinker warren's hill of salvaged trinkets is large enough to cut a door in.", 'The angriest of giants are often the most skillful weaponsmiths. Their grudges fuel endless sessions at the forge, all the while growling ferociously to themselves.', "The arbiter Galanda Feudkiller judges Lorwyn's squabbles from a lofty perspective.", 'The crone\'s boughs creaked as she spoke. "You look peaked, little one. Come, sip from my warm brew. It\'ll have you blooming in no time."', 'The dreams of giants are as long as time and as deep as the earth. Thus they are prized by the dream-harvesting fae.', 'The empathetic nature of the thoughtweft allows kithkin healers to treat the cause of an illness rather than fight its symptoms.', "The fae are so quick and their life spans so short that it's difficult to get retribution for their pranks.", "The fae know when they're not wanted. That's precisely why they show up.", 'The faultless and immaculate castes form the lower tiers of elvish society, with the exquisite caste above them. At the pinnacle is the perfect, a consummate blend of aristocrat and predator.', 'The flamekin are mere kindling for his warmth.', "The giants believe the fossils they find in Lorwyn's rocky heights are dreams frozen in time, and they treasure them.", 'The hardest lesson for any elf to learn is humility. It takes a giant to teach that.', 'The kith dance their elaborate reels not merely to celebrate the events of their lives but to form an unbreakable bond of loyalty with their kin, a bond stronger than the fear of death itself.', 'The knights are a major attraction at every Lammastide festival. Teams of riders perform daring feats of flight to the delight of all below.', 'The oil sloshes against his skull as he nears his destination: the Frogtosser Games and the lighting of the Flaming Boggart.', 'The only feeling greater than hurling something a mile is crushing something else with it that was really, really irritating you.', 'The scent of rot and vinegar fills the marsh, inviting boggarts from every warren to reunite and feast.', "The thoughtweft ties a clachan together. Sharing each other's hopes and fears, all the village's citizens spring into action upon the first threat to any one of them.", 'There is nowhere on Lorwyn that the Merrow Lanes cannot go.', 'They ride on waves of Æther, washing out anything that might pollute the Merrow Lanes.', "Though giants are mortal, they live so long and on such a grand scale that many small folk don't believe they ever truly die.", 'Though the currents of the Lanes shift every year, the merrow never lose track of where they are or where they are going.', 'Though they lack true flesh and bone of their own, changelings imitate either with equal ease.', 'Today it flies with the flock. Tomorrow it may wake to find them gone, its body in an unfamiliar form.', "Unaware of Lorwyn's diversity, it sees only itself, reflected a thousand times over.", 'Victims spirited through a faerie ring find themselves stranded miles away.', 'When a changeling adopts a form no other changeling has taken, a rune appears in the caverns of Velis Vel to mark the event.', 'When all is taken away, all are equal.', 'When he hits people, they stay hit.', "When provoked, a flamekin's inner fire burns far hotter than any giant's forge.", 'Winnowers live to eliminate eyeblights, creatures the elves deem too ugly to exist.']
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Alan Pollack', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Ben Thompson', 'Brandon Dorman', 'Carl Frank', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Chuck Lukacs', 'Cyril Van Der Haegen', 'Dan Dos Santos', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Dorman', 'Dominick Domingo', 'Eric Fortune', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Fred Fields', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Howard Lyon', 'Jeff Easley', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'Jim Pavelec', 'John Avon', 'John Franklin Howe', 'Kev Walker', 'Larry MacDougall', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Nils Hamm', 'Omar Rayyan', 'Paolo Parente', 'Paolo Parente & Brian Snõddy', 'Paul Chadwick', 'Pete Venters', 'Quinton Hoover', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Richard Sardinha', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ron Spears', 'Ron Spencer', 'Scott Hampton', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Steve Ellis', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Terese Nielsen & Philip Tan', 'Thomas Denmark', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne England', 'Wayne Reynolds', "William O'Connor", 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai']
